geowarden
=========

Accepts new connections on the public interfaces only from selected countries
(nftables table "inet geowarden", hook prerouting). Established connections,
VPN interfaces (e.g. Tailscale), Docker-internal traffic and the ports listed
in OPEN_TCP/OPEN_UDP are exempt.

Menu:           geowarden                          (as root)
Configuration:  /etc/geowarden.conf
Apply:          systemctl start geowarden.service  (or /usr/sbin/geowarden-apply)
Kill switch:    nft delete table inet geowarden    (until the next timer run)
Statistics:     geowarden -> Statistics and world map (start over after a reboot)
Updates:        geowarden.timer, at boot and daily
Geo data:       /var/cache/geowarden, monthly from DB-IP

Blocking is OFF after installation. Before turning it on, make sure you are
connecting from an allowed country or via an unfiltered interface (VPN).

Country data: "IP Geolocation by DB-IP" (https://db-ip.com), licensed under
CC BY 4.0. World map: Natural Earth (https://www.naturalearthdata.com), public domain.
